200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (The High Court accepted this contention and observed that Section 65\(7\) is couched in mandatory terms, clearly requiring the department to proceed under Sections 73 or 74 after completion of audit. The Court held that bypassing this adjudicatory mechanism and directly invoking revisional powers under Section 108 amounts to acting contrary to the scheme of the Act. Such an approach not only violates the statutory sequence but also deprives the assessee of the safeguards inherent in adjudication proceedings, including issuance of a show-cause notice, opportunity of reply and personal hearing. The Court further noted that Section 108 cannot be used to cure or substitute the absence of adjudication under Sections 73 or 74, and that revision of an audit report without following the prescribed process is illegal, arbitrary and without authority of law. Consequently, the revisional proceedings and the impugned order were quashed, and the writ petition was allowed.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
