/P 94 0 R
/E (What clearly emerges is that there is no blanket immunity available to taxpayers under Section 16\(2\)\(c\). Relief is conditional and fact-specific, available only where the recipient establishes bona fides and absence of fraud or collusion. This divergence of judicial views makes it inevitable that the Supreme Court will have to finally settle the law to ensure uniformity and certainty.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
