<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 95 0 R
/E (In the present case, the petitioner, a registered ISD, was subjected to audit proceedings where the department alleged wrongful availment and distribution of ISD credit on the ground that such credit had not been distributed within the same month, relying on Rule 39\(1\)\(a\). The petitioner challenged the proceedings contending that Section 20 of the CGST Act, which governs ISD mechanism, prescribes only the manner of distribution of credit and does not impose any time-limit. The petitioner argued that the Rule impermissibly curtailed a substantive statutory right by introducing a rigid monthly time-bar through delegated legislation. The High Court accepted this contention and observed that Section 20 does not contemplate any temporal restriction on ISD credit distribution. By prescribing a mandatory monthly limitation, Rule 39\(1\)\(a\) effectively extinguished a vested statutory entitlement, which is impermissible in delegated legislation. Relying on settled constitutional principles that rules cannot override or supplant the parent statute, the Court struck down Rule 39\(1\)\(a\) as being beyond the scope of Section 20.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
239 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 95 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
