398 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (On the issue of refund, the Court took note of the fact that the petitioner had paid the disputed amount under protest during investigation/enforcement proceedings. The Court reiterated that such payments, extracted in the course of investigation and without adjudication, cannot be regarded as voluntary. Since the levy itself was found to be without authority of law, the Court held that retention of such amount by the department would offend Article 265 of the Constitution. Accordingly, the respondents were directed to refund the amount collected, along with interest at the rate of 6% per annum, from the date of collection till the date of refund, thereby granting complete relief to the petitioner.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
399 0 obj
<<
