>>
endobj
419 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 104 0 R
/E (This ruling brings important clarity on the taxability of centage charges, a recurring area of dispute for Government undertakings and public sector entities engaged in supervisory and consultancy roles. By reaffirming that supervision and project management services, without any element of goods supply or works contract, constitute pure services, the Kerala AAR has aligned with a consistent line of rulings in the case of Structures India ANZ Project Management Services Pvt. Ltd. \(Advance Ruling No. KER/140/2021 dt. 25.06.2022\). )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
420 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 104 0 R
/E (At the same time, the ruling serves as a cautionary reminder on refund limitation. Even where a levy is subsequently held to be exempt, refund claims must strictly comply with Section 54 timelines. Advance Ruling Authorities have consistently declined to dilute statutory limitation, leaving taxpayers to pursue alternative remedies before constitutional courts in appropriate cases. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
